From 5e06a945f97893662a8a8bb3063f307cf70da7e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:31:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 105/137] ASoC: qdsp6: q6voice: Set up CVD 2.3 vocprocs from
 the back ends

CVD 2.3 and later (CVP API version 2) want a vocproc to be created with
CREATE_FULL_CONTROL_SESSION_V3 and then told the channels of each side
and the media format of its AFE port before the topology is committed.
The sequence added for SDM670 used a fixed format (48 kHz, 16 bit, one
TX and two RX channels), was selected by a DT property only, ignored
every error, and the endpoint media format packet put its channel map
at the offset of the channel info structure, with the port id as the
channel count.

- q6cvp reads the CVP API version from q6core when it probes and logs
  it. The V3 sequence stays the choice of the qcom,cvd-v2.3 property: on
  SM8350 (CVD 2.3, CVP API version 2.0) V3 brings the downlink up but the
  uplink stays silent, while V2, where the DSP takes the formats from the
  AFE ports itself, carries a call both ways.
- One SET_PARAM_V2 helper builds the in-band parameter packets; the
  channel info and endpoint format take the channels, bits and rate.
- The path starts at prepare instead of startup: by then the back ends
  have their (fixed-up) hw_params and their AFE ports run. The DAI
  passes the parameters of the back end whose port the path uses.
- A path without a port selected passes VSS_IVOCPROC_PORT_ID_NONE, not
  the port of DAI id 0, and unselecting a port no longer selects that
  one either.
- Every step is checked, and a vocproc that failed is released.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
